1
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:07,070
Can I court you, Time?

2
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:13,000
But I'll forget everything before

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,400
and get to know you all over again.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,070
This is the last time.

5
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:18,100
Do it right.

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,470
I don't want to hurt again.

7
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:21,600
Do you know everywhere I looked for you?

8
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,170
You weren't fucking anywhere.

9
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:26,130
I'm starting to fear my love will hurt you again.

10
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,430
I love you, too.

11
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:30,570
It's me! / Hey!

12
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:31,630
Your snack guy.

13
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:32,770
I don't like this!

14
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:34,100
You psycho!

15
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,730
Then why'd you cheat on me with him?

16
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:40,430
But it doesn't matter anymore, because today you're mine.

17
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,530
What the fuck, you bastard?

18
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:43,870
Star.

19
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:45,400
Din...

20
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:49,000
I'm sorry I'm late.

21
00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:51,330
Thanks for helping Star, man.

22
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:52,470
He's my brother too.

23
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:54,600
All I thought was, I can't die yet.

24
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:56,630
I still want to wake up to you.

25
00:00:56,630 --> 00:00:57,700
Small as you are,

26
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,700
how are you this strong?

27
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,100
I promise I'll take good care of you.

28
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,500
I'll get in through the quota round.

29
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,400
Fine. But I have one more condition.

30
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,570
If you don't get in this round,

31
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:11,800
you'll go to the university I choose

32
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,170
and the faculty I pick.

33
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:14,900
Do you understand me, Din?

34
00:01:18,270 --> 00:01:22,330
"Not selected"

35
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:25,730
Not applying for med?

36
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:27,000
Let me have this, Mom.

37
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:29,470
You really want to study here?

38
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:32,630
If you want to decide, you have to deliver.

39
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,870
"Time, tell Star for me that I didn't get in this round."

40
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:50,600
"But don't overthink it. I'll get in through the quota round."

41
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,030
"I'll be busier, but I won't disappear."

42
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:55,430
"Please understand."

43
00:02:05,030 --> 00:02:08,130
"Star's read it. He asked me to send you this picture."

44
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,330
Your future matters to me.

45
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:13,430
Give it your all.

46
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:16,870
I'll take good care of myself, for you too.

47
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,600
Confess.

48
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:45,670
Shit, how did I never figure that out?

49
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:48,600
This is fucking news to me.

50
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,230
Not just you.

51
00:04:51,230 --> 00:04:54,130
I always thought he liked Tonnam.

52
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,900
What about him?

53
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:58,370
Does he like you?

54
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,670
Well, if I'm not just kidding myself,

55
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:12,470
I don't think he finds me annoying.

56
00:05:12,470 --> 00:05:14,430
He just needs some time to think.

57
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:17,800
I've been watching Time for a year now.

58
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:20,600
I know what he likes and doesn't like,

59
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,530
what makes him happy.

60
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:26,300
I love how well he takes care of himself.

61
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:30,070
I just want to take care of him even better.

62
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:35,130
With this one, I'm dead serious.

63
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:49,500
I know you can do it, man.

64
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:54,030
The thing is, how much is Time going to open up to you?

65
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,230
No idea.

66
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:00,170
But I don't want to pressure him.

67
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:03,470
Same as you, right?

68
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:06,200
For me, I've already told him how I feel.

69
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:08,200
If he hasn't shut the door,

70
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,730
I still have hope.

71
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:11,570
At least Time seems smart.

72
00:06:11,570 --> 00:06:12,770
Unlike Fuen.

73
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:14,230
A year of hints,

74
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:15,330
and still nothing.

75
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:17,330
Sure, Mr. Perfect.

76
00:06:17,330 --> 00:06:19,330
Like you've never screwed up.

77
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:21,630
A one-man show and a hat-trick,

78
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:24,070
plus two more for five goals, right?

79
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:25,970
Ow!

80
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:28,970
But I seriously respect you, Physics,

81
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,900
for never giving up on Fuen.

82
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,030
What can I do?

83
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:39,600
I already fell for him.

84
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,670
But you and Time,

85
00:06:45,670 --> 00:06:48,900
give it long enough and it'll be the same for you.

86
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,600
Are you going to give up first?

87
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:55,870
I don't think so.

88
00:06:57,670 --> 00:06:59,830
Unless he tells me to stop.

89
00:07:03,770 --> 00:07:06,800
Students, get ready to present. Stop playing now.

90
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,270
Hey, play it right this time, okay?

91
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:22,230
Give it your all. I'm recording.

92
00:07:23,270 --> 00:07:26,570
Hey, wait. When the clip opens,

93
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:29,400
backs turned first, then turn when the music hits?

94
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:34,000
When we perform for real, if we put a lot of feeling into it, it'll be amazing.

95
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,600
Hey, Art. That solo part,

96
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,800
make it more hype. It'll be fun.

97
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:39,570
Got it.

98
00:07:39,570 --> 00:07:40,570
Let's go!

99
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,430
3, 2, 1.

100
00:08:05,670 --> 00:08:11,100
♪ Have you ever felt it — no matter how far the days carry us ♪

101
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:15,370
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on the story of that day ♪

102
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:22,200
♪ it warms my heart all over again ♪

103
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:28,330
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

104
00:08:28,330 --> 00:08:32,630
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

105
00:08:32,630 --> 00:08:37,770
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

106
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:47,570
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

107
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:56,200
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

108
00:08:56,200 --> 00:09:00,300
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

109
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:04,370
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

110
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:08,670
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

111
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:13,430
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

112
00:09:13,430 --> 00:09:17,530
♪ It's all still so clear, it never faded ♪

113
00:09:17,530 --> 00:09:21,770
♪ Even if today we have to go our separate ways ♪

114
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:26,170
♪ However far apart you and I may be ♪

115
00:09:26,170 --> 00:09:30,070
♪ our time together is still here in my heart ♪

116
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:34,370
♪ It's all still so clear ♪

117
00:09:35,970 --> 00:09:42,330
♪ I'm only just learning what it's like without you ♪

118
00:09:42,330 --> 00:09:46,230
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

119
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:53,070
♪ those days make me miss you, my dear ♪

120
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:09,800
Woo!

121
00:10:33,630 --> 00:10:34,870
Tired?

122
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:43,130
Yeah... but I want to finish this page first.

123
00:10:51,630 --> 00:10:53,430
If we go to England,

124
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,070
what do you want to do?

125
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:04,870
Ride the bus.

126
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,570
Isn't that a train?

127
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:13,500
I don't know.

128
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:15,200
I've never been.

129
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:22,600
But I want to see how people live there.

130
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:27,230
What else?

131
00:11:31,730 --> 00:11:39,430
Walk around town and take photos. But you're taking mine.

132
00:11:42,830 --> 00:11:50,300
And a market tour. But promise me

133
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:53,500
you'll help me save. Don't eat too much.

134
00:11:56,570 --> 00:11:57,730
Deal.

135
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:03,670
Is there anywhere you especially want to go?

136
00:12:12,330 --> 00:12:13,330
A church.

137
00:12:17,270 --> 00:12:19,530
I want to go to a church with you.

138
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:32,400
Hmm. But what you just said,

139
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:36,000
I... don't get what you mean.

140
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,970
But wherever you go, I'm ready to go too.

141
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:47,800
I mean everywhere you just mentioned.

142
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,500
I'll go with you.

143
00:13:05,230 --> 00:13:07,770
So, is it the train or the bus?

144
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:09,430
You'll find out.

145
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:11,200
Let me pass the interview first.

146
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:41,500
Guys, should we send the clip now?

147
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:47,230
Send it. They say today's an auspicious day, perfect for competing.

148
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:48,930
Based on whose horoscope?

149
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:49,930
Thanop's.

150
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:52,630
Huh? Why not check your own?

151
00:13:52,630 --> 00:13:55,600
Oh, I did. I'm doomed.

152
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:58,800
What about Jet's and Art's?

153
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,870
Ugh, even worse than mine.

154
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:01,770
Seriously?

155
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:03,530
Where are those two now?

156
00:14:03,530 --> 00:14:05,570
They probably rushed off to tutoring.

157
00:14:05,930 --> 00:14:08,370
So whose luck do we use to enter the contest?

158
00:14:08,370 --> 00:14:09,370
Good point.

159
00:14:12,070 --> 00:14:14,070
Mine's not bad.

160
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:17,800
But I should watch out for breaking things.

161
00:14:18,470 --> 00:14:20,730
But entering can't break anything.

162
00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:21,770
Yeah, easy.

163
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:22,800
Here we go!

164
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:26,270
Let's do this!

165
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:53,930
There you are. I've been looking all over for you.

166
00:14:55,430 --> 00:14:57,330
When will you stop using

167
00:14:57,330 --> 00:14:59,300
council perks to study here so late?

168
00:15:00,930 --> 00:15:02,700
Studying at home is way better.

169
00:15:03,130 --> 00:15:07,330
Hmm, I think it's chill here. More comfortable.

170
00:15:07,330 --> 00:15:11,200
The school closes at seven. Going home late is dangerous.

171
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:14,300
I'll think about it.

172
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:17,130
But I still don't like studying at home.

173
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:20,700
Or do you have a place you'd recommend?

174
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,770
Your friend's place?

175
00:15:28,470 --> 00:15:30,670
My friends are all taken.

176
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:36,730
Then, from now on, whenever you study at school,

177
00:15:36,730 --> 00:15:38,130
I'll come keep you company.

178
00:15:42,730 --> 00:15:43,830
Thank you.

179
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:45,800
Hungry?

180
00:15:46,130 --> 00:15:47,770
I'll get you something to eat.

181
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:50,030
Whoa, Time!

182
00:15:54,030 --> 00:15:55,600
Before looking after others,

183
00:15:56,770 --> 00:15:58,970
stop being so clumsy first.

184
00:16:05,730 --> 00:16:07,500
Come on, I'm hungry.

185
00:16:38,930 --> 00:16:40,570
I'd better head home.

186
00:16:42,070 --> 00:16:43,530
See you, see you.

187
00:16:43,530 --> 00:16:45,570
Get home safe. Bye-bye.

188
00:16:45,570 --> 00:16:47,000
Bye.

189
00:16:50,270 --> 00:16:51,670
Yeah, see you.

190
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:53,770
Get home safe.

191
00:16:55,900 --> 00:17:01,530
Why didn't you tell me you were coming? What if I'd left already?

192
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:04,000
Then I guess I'd get surprised back.

193
00:17:04,599 --> 00:17:06,000
That's not okay, Aof.

194
00:17:06,270 --> 00:17:09,369
Next time, you tell me before you come. Got it?

195
00:17:10,069 --> 00:17:12,970
Yes... I get it.

196
00:17:15,569 --> 00:17:18,099
Next time, I'll tell you first.

197
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Good boy.

198
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,030
So how was practice today? Tired?

199
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,069
Ugh, ugh, ugh.

200
00:17:31,530 --> 00:17:34,270
I'm so tired.

201
00:17:38,070 --> 00:17:42,370
But we sent the clip just in time.

202
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:46,470
Whoa.

203
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:50,370
I should've gone up and listened outside.

204
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:52,500
I missed hearing you sing again.

205
00:17:53,730 --> 00:17:54,730
Then...

206
00:17:55,730 --> 00:17:57,230
Want me to sing for you?

207
00:17:58,230 --> 00:17:59,230
Really?

208
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,170
Yeah, really.

209
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:04,330
Okay, pick a song.

210
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:07,100
If it's your voice,

211
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:08,700
any song is fine.

212
00:18:13,230 --> 00:18:14,630
Then...

213
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:17,870
Hold on.

214
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:36,400
This one, then.

215
00:18:41,670 --> 00:18:49,470
♪ ...you gave me, that day we sat side by side ♪

216
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:59,030
♪ We once made a promise that we'd have each other ♪

217
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:11,200
♪ That day everything seemed so clear, we laughed all day ♪

218
00:19:12,770 --> 00:19:17,530
♪ that I still remember now ♪

219
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:30,900
♪ Because this heart of mine is still waiting, only for you ♪

220
00:19:40,670 --> 00:19:42,570
I wrote this song myself.

221
00:19:44,870 --> 00:19:46,970
It's not finished yet,

222
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,700
but I wanted you to hear it first.

223
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:53,800
Thank you.

224
00:19:55,430 --> 00:19:59,600
I don't know why, but... all of a sudden...

225
00:20:00,130 --> 00:20:02,270
the tears just started coming.

226
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:05,730
There, there.

227
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,900
Such a crybaby.

228
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:17,470
I'll finish this song and make it complete.

229
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:20,000
And when that day comes,

230
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,600
don't forget to let me hear it first.

231
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,300
I won't forget.

232
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:26,270
Promise.

233
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,670
Thank you, Chemi.

234
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:40,500
Can you play it for me one more time?

235
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,230
You're welcome.

236
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,500
Let me lean on you.

237
00:21:41,330 --> 00:21:43,700
You have tutoring at school today, right?

238
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:48,470
I'll drop you off. I have errands around there anyway.

239
00:21:50,370 --> 00:21:51,470
Okay, Mom.

240
00:21:51,970 --> 00:21:54,870
When do you finish? I'll pick you up if I can.

241
00:21:54,870 --> 00:21:58,600
Probably evening, Mom. I'm meeting Chok and Tonnam to keep studying.

242
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:01,270
I see. Will you be home for dinner?

243
00:22:01,270 --> 00:22:02,830
Don't wait for me, Mom.

244
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:05,400
I'll probably eat before I come home.

245
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,430
Let me eat quickly, then I'll take you.

246
00:22:07,430 --> 00:22:08,230
Okay, Mom.

247
00:22:08,230 --> 00:22:08,870
Okay.

248
00:22:09,930 --> 00:22:11,470
Attention, all M.6 students.

249
00:22:11,470 --> 00:22:15,730
After school today, the guidance counselor will be giving university advice.

250
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,170
Hey, Time.

251
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:23,300
You've been getting home late

252
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,770
because you stay up with Tang while he studies?

253
00:22:26,330 --> 00:22:28,800
Yeah. You're never free when we ask anymore,

254
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,470
but you're with Tang everywhere.

255
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,570
So, in conclusion,

256
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:34,500
you like Tang, right?

257
00:22:38,630 --> 00:22:40,400
Anything to say in your defense?

258
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,130
Otherwise, the court rules that...

259
00:22:42,870 --> 00:22:44,770
you like him.

260
00:22:46,630 --> 00:22:47,630
I confess.

261
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:48,970
Lock me up.

262
00:22:48,970 --> 00:22:50,770
The defendant turns himself in.

263
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:53,200
But give me a little more time to think.

264
00:22:54,070 --> 00:22:56,230
Time, where are you going to get more time?

265
00:22:56,230 --> 00:22:58,300
Tang's about to graduate, you know.

266
00:22:58,300 --> 00:22:59,600
Yeah.

267
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:03,370
So let him graduate. Then I'll know if he changes his mind.

268
00:23:03,370 --> 00:23:04,900
You can play hard to get,

269
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:06,500
but if he gives up,

270
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:08,700
you'll be the one moping.

271
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,970
Yeah. Good guys don't come along that often these days.

272
00:23:11,970 --> 00:23:15,170
Let Tang slip away, and who knows if you'll find another.

273
00:23:15,170 --> 00:23:19,000
Honestly, Time, we're rooting for Tang.

274
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,670
Ever since you met him,

275
00:23:20,670 --> 00:23:23,530
you've looked so happy, you know?

276
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:25,830
I know.

277
00:23:26,330 --> 00:23:28,570
I know myself. When I'm with Tang,

278
00:23:28,570 --> 00:23:30,270
I'm so damn happy.

279
00:23:30,930 --> 00:23:34,570
But I want to stay with this feeling a little longer.

280
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:38,500
I'm just not sure

281
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,930
if what I'm feeling

282
00:23:39,930 --> 00:23:42,530
is because I really like him, or...

283
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,030
just because he's being nice to me.

284
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:50,100
Damn, that's deep.

285
00:23:55,270 --> 00:23:57,200
I know you look after yourself,

286
00:23:57,200 --> 00:24:00,500
but let me care for you better.

287
00:24:06,270 --> 00:24:08,370
I like him!

288
00:24:08,370 --> 00:24:10,600
Yeah, we know.

289
00:24:21,130 --> 00:24:22,730
How was today?

290
00:24:23,730 --> 00:24:24,730
Chill.

291
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,370
I could take the exam tomorrow.

292
00:24:26,670 --> 00:24:28,070
Good to be confident.

293
00:24:28,070 --> 00:24:29,470
Want to see a movie?

294
00:24:29,470 --> 00:24:30,370
Got tickets.

295
00:24:30,370 --> 00:24:31,200
Sure.

296
00:24:32,030 --> 00:24:33,400
Ooh, look at you two.

297
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,030
Where are you off to?

298
00:24:35,030 --> 00:24:36,030
Butt out.

299
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:37,830
Just kidding.

300
00:24:37,830 --> 00:24:38,830
Okay.

301
00:24:39,770 --> 00:24:41,100
What about you guys?

302
00:24:41,100 --> 00:24:42,170
Going to a movie.

303
00:24:42,170 --> 00:24:44,270
Hey, we're going to see a movie too.

304
00:24:45,030 --> 00:24:46,070
Which one?

305
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,400
This one.

306
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,400
Hey!

307
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:52,970
Same movie.

308
00:24:52,970 --> 00:24:55,130
Oh, great. Let's go.

309
00:24:55,130 --> 00:24:57,100
Let's go, come on.

310
00:25:09,570 --> 00:25:11,130
This one looks good too.

311
00:25:12,270 --> 00:25:14,530
This one's better. It's trending right now.

312
00:25:14,530 --> 00:25:16,730
Four seats, please.

313
00:25:17,170 --> 00:25:19,470
Yeah, I want to see the same one as Time.

314
00:25:19,470 --> 00:25:21,000
Yeah, this one's fine.

315
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,600
Oh, Star.

316
00:25:26,930 --> 00:25:28,270
Oh, Din.

317
00:25:28,270 --> 00:25:29,830
You're here for a movie too?

318
00:25:29,830 --> 00:25:30,930
Yes.

319
00:25:31,830 --> 00:25:33,530
Same movie as us?

320
00:25:34,030 --> 00:25:36,900
Of course. I already booked online.

321
00:25:39,870 --> 00:25:42,000
I booked. He didn't.

322
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,730
Same thing.

323
00:25:48,130 --> 00:25:51,630
Nice. We didn't come together, but we're watching together.

324
00:25:51,630 --> 00:25:53,470
It's totally fate.

325
00:25:56,900 --> 00:25:59,770
Okay, come on. Let's go!

326
00:27:05,730 --> 00:27:10,230
Trust me, this place is really good. It's famous around here.

327
00:27:10,230 --> 00:27:11,830
Star, what do you want?

328
00:27:11,830 --> 00:27:13,200
Whatever you like.

329
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:15,730
Their desserts are amazing here.

330
00:27:15,730 --> 00:27:17,670
What do you like to eat?

331
00:27:17,670 --> 00:27:19,070
I like...

332
00:27:42,030 --> 00:27:44,770
Your mom doesn't know about Star at all?

333
00:27:46,030 --> 00:27:47,830
I never told her.

334
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:51,700
I've never seen Aunt Om like this.

335
00:27:52,330 --> 00:27:54,530
It's going to be okay, right, Din?

336
00:27:54,970 --> 00:27:57,030
That's so scary.

337
00:27:58,100 --> 00:27:59,700
I don't know.

338
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:27,170
Din, I think everything your mom said is right.

339
00:28:28,070 --> 00:28:29,600
What matters most for you now

340
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:32,300
is focusing on university.

341
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:40,430
I think we should take some space,

342
00:28:40,430 --> 00:28:42,300
until you get into a school.

343
00:28:45,030 --> 00:28:47,570
Wait, I already told you...

344
00:28:47,570 --> 00:28:49,570
Din, we're going home.

345
00:28:50,330 --> 00:28:53,300
No, Mom. We already talked about this.

346
00:28:53,830 --> 00:28:55,430
Why are you doing this?

347
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:56,930
What did you tell Star?

348
00:28:56,930 --> 00:28:59,230
Your mom didn't say anything bad.

349
00:28:59,670 --> 00:29:01,600
This was all my idea.

350
00:29:03,070 --> 00:29:04,530
You know what?

351
00:29:05,070 --> 00:29:09,130
Your future means a lot to me.

352
00:29:09,130 --> 00:29:12,930
And if... being in your life makes it worse,

353
00:29:13,530 --> 00:29:14,900
I don't want to be in it.

354
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:18,430
Star, you don't make my life worse.

355
00:29:19,470 --> 00:29:21,270
Can't I make one mistake, Mom?

356
00:29:21,430 --> 00:29:22,430
I messed up.

357
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:24,030
I know.

358
00:29:25,530 --> 00:29:27,900
But I'm trying to make it work.

359
00:29:28,470 --> 00:29:30,830
Din, I've always listened to you.

360
00:29:30,830 --> 00:29:33,770
Whenever you said you'd do something, you did it.

361
00:29:34,030 --> 00:29:37,130
But this time, I just want to know if you failed

362
00:29:37,770 --> 00:29:39,770
because you can't balance your love life

363
00:29:39,770 --> 00:29:41,870
with your own life.

364
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:47,700
Then you have to prove

365
00:29:47,700 --> 00:29:49,800
that your mom is wrong.

366
00:29:51,100 --> 00:29:54,900
Because in the end, I don't want us to end like this either.

367
00:30:03,600 --> 00:30:04,830
Yes, Mom.

368
00:30:05,430 --> 00:30:06,630
I understand.

369
00:30:07,270 --> 00:30:09,070
And I'll prove it to you.

370
00:30:15,100 --> 00:30:18,600
Star, trust me.

371
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:28,870
Star.

372
00:30:30,430 --> 00:30:32,170
I want to ask you something.

373
00:30:35,030 --> 00:30:36,730
What is it?

374
00:30:42,470 --> 00:30:44,230
If we have to be apart...

375
00:30:44,230 --> 00:30:47,230
could you post stories so I can see

376
00:30:47,230 --> 00:30:51,330
what you're up to? So I won't worry.

377
00:30:59,100 --> 00:31:00,800
Thank you.

378
00:31:38,630 --> 00:31:40,430
How was your day, Aof?

379
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:43,230
I'd rather hear about yours.

380
00:31:43,430 --> 00:31:44,430
So today, right,

381
00:31:44,430 --> 00:31:47,630
Thanop and I went out for shabu.

382
00:31:47,630 --> 00:31:51,030
Then I told Thanop to check if the pot was hot yet.

383
00:31:51,030 --> 00:31:54,270
He grabbed the pot and blistered his hand like this.

384
00:31:54,270 --> 00:31:55,530
I was so confused.

385
00:31:55,530 --> 00:31:58,370
Instead of the pork, he put his own hand on it.

386
00:31:58,370 --> 00:31:59,370
He screamed!

387
00:31:59,370 --> 00:32:00,730
Like a monkey, Chemi.

388
00:32:00,730 --> 00:32:03,170
Then he ran off and jumped into the canal.

389
00:32:03,570 --> 00:32:05,670
It was so damn funny. I even filmed it.

390
00:32:05,670 --> 00:32:08,030
I'll show you the clip when we see each other.

391
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Chemi?

392
00:32:21,570 --> 00:32:22,570
Chemi?

393
00:32:24,870 --> 00:32:26,200
Did you fall asleep?

394
00:32:28,530 --> 00:32:29,530
Chemi?

395
00:32:33,330 --> 00:32:35,070
Sweet dreams, Chemi.

396
00:33:09,130 --> 00:33:10,130
Din.

397
00:33:10,730 --> 00:33:12,400
Don't overdo it, sweetie.

398
00:33:19,500 --> 00:33:21,000
Mom.

399
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:24,870
I'm not mad at you, Mom.

400
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:31,100
But I want you to give Star a chance.

401
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:34,530
It doesn't have to be now.

402
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:36,900
Just let me get in first.

403
00:33:39,030 --> 00:33:40,900
Study hard, sweetie.

404
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:31,130
Want some water, man?

405
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:33,530
Let's get to the point.

406
00:34:39,300 --> 00:34:40,300
How are you doing?

407
00:34:43,270 --> 00:34:44,670
I'm okay.

408
00:34:45,770 --> 00:34:47,469
Hey.

409
00:34:48,429 --> 00:34:49,969
Did you fight with your mom?

410
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,800
Did she lay a hand on you?

411
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,929
Are you hurt anywhere?

412
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:56,270
I'm worried about you, man.

413
00:34:59,330 --> 00:35:00,870
Why would we fight?

414
00:35:00,870 --> 00:35:02,370
We already talked it out.

415
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:05,400
I'm really fine.

416
00:35:06,430 --> 00:35:08,500
Once the exam's over, it'll all be over.

417
00:35:12,100 --> 00:35:13,700
So since that day,

418
00:35:13,700 --> 00:35:15,770
you haven't talked to your little star?

419
00:35:19,900 --> 00:35:21,170
Little star?

420
00:35:22,270 --> 00:35:23,470
Din's little star.

421
00:35:23,470 --> 00:35:25,500
Not Patrick Star, okay?

422
00:35:28,370 --> 00:35:29,830
Are we done here?

423
00:35:29,830 --> 00:35:32,170
Then let me study for my future.

424
00:35:33,400 --> 00:35:34,900
Then we've got futures too.

425
00:35:34,900 --> 00:35:36,130
We'll study with you.

426
00:36:47,270 --> 00:36:49,500
"FUN VIBE / Thapfah Wittayanusorn School"

427
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:58,570
Round two.

428
00:37:00,300 --> 00:37:04,100
Each band has to perform three songs.

429
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:07,470
One of them has to be an original.

430
00:37:09,870 --> 00:37:11,300
Who's going to write it?

431
00:37:11,300 --> 00:37:12,700
Who's writing?

432
00:37:14,330 --> 00:37:17,170
Actually, I have a song I've written.

433
00:37:17,170 --> 00:37:18,730
It might not be good yet.

434
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:23,230
Let me hear it.

435
00:37:23,230 --> 00:37:24,970
Please, can we hear it?

436
00:38:13,900 --> 00:38:15,500
Physics. / Hmm?

437
00:38:15,500 --> 00:38:17,400
Is this one good enough?

438
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:19,630
It's good. Put it in the portfolio.

439
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:28,800
What about this sketch?

440
00:38:29,200 --> 00:38:30,200
Physics.

441
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:34,330
That's great. Go for it, keep it.

442
00:38:34,930 --> 00:38:36,970
Okay. / Let's go, let's go!

443
00:38:53,230 --> 00:38:55,830
Okay, got it.

444
00:39:03,930 --> 00:39:05,830
Every piece is so beautiful.

445
00:39:06,130 --> 00:39:07,500
With skills like this,

446
00:39:08,100 --> 00:39:09,830
just wait. You'll pass for sure.

447
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:11,970
Is it really good?

448
00:39:12,900 --> 00:39:13,900
Of course.

449
00:39:14,330 --> 00:39:16,030
Anyone who sees it will say so.

450
00:39:20,730 --> 00:39:21,970
What's wrong?

451
00:39:23,330 --> 00:39:26,030
Smile. Come on, smile.

452
00:39:28,900 --> 00:39:35,770
Be confident. Believe in yourself. Okay? It'll be fine either way.

453
00:39:35,770 --> 00:39:40,830
♪ When you turn to me, I can't hold your gaze for long ♪

454
00:39:40,830 --> 00:39:46,470
♪ I carry it into my dreams each night, but I can't do a thing about it ♪

455
00:39:46,470 --> 00:39:51,730
♪ Every look you send my way makes my heart shake even more ♪

456
00:39:51,730 --> 00:39:56,000
♪ One slip and I'm imagining things ♪

457
00:39:56,800 --> 00:40:02,270
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day ♪

458
00:40:02,270 --> 00:40:07,500
♪ My heart can't take it ♪

459
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:13,030
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

460
00:40:13,030 --> 00:40:18,530
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

461
00:40:18,530 --> 00:40:23,870
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

462
00:40:23,870 --> 00:40:28,570
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

463
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:20,630
"Can you come down for a bit? I'm waiting outside your house."

464
00:42:01,030 --> 00:42:02,700
Dad, Mom...

465
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:05,370
I'm heading out. Bye.

466
00:42:05,370 --> 00:42:06,570
Bye.

467
00:42:18,530 --> 00:42:19,300
Hold this.

468
00:42:37,370 --> 00:42:39,070
Very good.

469
00:42:55,370 --> 00:42:59,200
Sit tight, okay? Don't let go when I take off.

470
00:43:00,230 --> 00:43:01,670
Spread your arms.

471
00:43:27,330 --> 00:43:29,500
You're the one who taught me this.

472
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:33,270
Yeah, yeah.

473
00:43:35,170 --> 00:43:37,130
Okay, we're leaving.

474
00:43:37,130 --> 00:43:38,500
Good luck, sweetie.

475
00:43:38,500 --> 00:43:39,970
Bye.

476
00:43:39,970 --> 00:43:40,970
Bye, son.

477
00:43:40,970 --> 00:43:42,630
Even if you guess, guess right.

478
00:43:42,630 --> 00:43:44,470
You got it! / Yes.

479
00:44:21,630 --> 00:44:23,270
Here.

480
00:44:32,030 --> 00:44:33,670
What's wrong?

481
00:44:33,670 --> 00:44:35,700
Nervous?

482
00:44:52,500 --> 00:44:55,130
Whatever's going on in your head right now,

483
00:44:55,130 --> 00:44:56,830
leave it all behind.

484
00:44:58,970 --> 00:45:01,030
Just go in and focus on the exam.

485
00:45:11,400 --> 00:45:13,400
I know you can do it.

486
00:45:21,030 --> 00:45:22,200
Don't worry.

487
00:45:34,470 --> 00:45:36,870
No matter what, I'll be right here by your side.

488
00:46:14,500 --> 00:46:15,900
Thinking about Din?

489
00:46:17,530 --> 00:46:18,530
Yeah.

490
00:46:19,730 --> 00:46:22,330
I still don't know how he's doing.

491
00:46:26,030 --> 00:46:28,500
How many exams does he have left?

492
00:46:30,930 --> 00:46:32,500
Two, I think.

493
00:46:34,670 --> 00:46:36,070
Hold it right there.

494
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:37,830
Star.

495
00:46:41,670 --> 00:46:43,100
Sneaking photos again?

496
00:46:43,430 --> 00:46:46,270
Perfect timing. I'll send it to Din

497
00:46:46,270 --> 00:46:48,370
to cheer him on for his exam.

498
00:47:01,730 --> 00:47:04,170
The morning exam is about to begin.

499
00:47:04,170 --> 00:47:06,000
Please get ready.

500
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:08,970
The papers will be handed out in ten minutes.

501
00:47:40,900 --> 00:47:42,930
Time's up. Everyone, pens down.

502
00:47:46,570 --> 00:47:49,970
The afternoon exam starts at 1:30 p.m.

503
00:47:49,970 --> 00:47:53,530
Please be on time. Thank you.

504
00:48:25,830 --> 00:48:28,330
I want something of yours

505
00:48:29,030 --> 00:48:30,770
to keep with me.

506
00:48:30,770 --> 00:48:32,570
Can you give me something?

507
00:49:42,330 --> 00:49:43,600
Dad!

508
00:50:02,030 --> 00:50:05,170
"I won't say my son isn't capable. I know you're the best."

509
00:50:05,170 --> 00:50:08,400
"I'm proud, but you're focused on the wrong thing. (Din's mom)"

510
00:50:08,400 --> 00:50:10,500
"You know who I am and how I think."

511
00:50:10,500 --> 00:50:12,100
"I can't lose you. So..."

512
00:50:12,100 --> 00:50:13,770
"stay with me. Promise? (Fuen)"

513
00:50:13,770 --> 00:50:14,900
"Promise. (Physics)"

514
00:50:14,900 --> 00:50:16,970
"I don't want to hold you back. (Star)"

515
00:50:16,970 --> 00:50:19,200
"You keep me going, not back. (Din)"

516
00:50:19,200 --> 00:50:21,300
"Show her I make you better. (Star)"

517
00:50:21,670 --> 00:50:22,830
Look forward to it.

518
00:50:22,830 --> 00:50:23,930
I'll listen closely.

519
00:50:24,500 --> 00:50:26,800
You're from Thapfah, right?

520
00:50:27,300 --> 00:50:30,470
Yes. / Thapfah Wittayanusorn.

521
00:50:34,600 --> 00:50:36,470
Your mom told me everything,

522
00:50:36,470 --> 00:50:37,770
about the exam and Star.

523
00:50:37,770 --> 00:50:39,000
Was I wrong, Dad?

524
00:50:39,000 --> 00:50:41,900
Din, let's go see your mom.

525
00:50:44,900 --> 00:50:47,330
You know, right? But you shouldn't have, Star.

526
00:50:47,800 --> 00:50:49,630
Why did the university email me?

527
00:50:49,630 --> 00:50:51,300
An offer from the university?

528
00:50:51,300 --> 00:50:52,600
I'm not ready for this.

529
00:50:52,600 --> 00:50:54,030
I can't bear to look.
